.\" Leon Bootloader — Man Page
.TH LBL 1 "2026-08-02" "lbl 0.7.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lbl \- the Leon chainloading bootloader for Cudane
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lbl
.br
(EFI application \fIlbl.efi\fR; booted directly by the UEFI firmware)
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lbl
is the UEFI bootloader for the Leon project. It runs in the firmware
environment, captures the GOP framebuffer without ever calling \fBset_mode\fR,
parses the ACPI BGRT logo table, discovers the boot entries on the EFI System
Partition, and chainloads the chosen image with
.BR LoadImage " / " StartImage .
It has no command-line interface: it is launched by the firmware from an EFI
System Partition and runs during boot. Any terminal invocation simply reports
that it is not an EFI environment.
.SH BOOT SEQUENCE
.TP
1
Resolve the system tables and verify a UEFI environment.
.TP
2
Capture the Graphics Output Protocol framebuffer (current mode only; no
.B set_mode
so the graphics hardware is never re-initialized) and record its geometry
(resolution, stride, pixel format).
.TP
3
Walk the ACPI tables, parse the BGRT, and capture the logo rectangle, status,
and image type.
.TP
4
Read and validate the boot configuration \eEFI\eleon\eboot.toml (written by
.BR "lbc config set" );
a missing or broken file yields defaults, never a blocked boot.
.TP
5
Discover every \eEFI\e\e*.efi boot entry and write them as JSONC to
\eEFI\eleon\eentries.jsonc.
.TP
6
Record the live geometry + resolved config to \eEFI\eleon\ebootinfo.json for
host-side tooling.
.TP
7
With \fBsplash = true\fR, show a menu; otherwise boot the configured
\fBdefault_entry\fR, falling back to the first discovered entry.
.TP
8
Chainload the chosen image via
.BR LoadImage " / " StartImage
with
.BR BootPolicy::BootSelection ,
without touching the screen. The kernel (an EFI stub) then does its own GOP +
BGRT acquisition, calls \fBexit_boot_services()\fR itself, and halts.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I \eEFI\eleon\eleon.efi
The bootloader application (also staged as \eEFI\eBOOT\ebootx64\e.efi).
.TP
.I \eEFI\eleon\ekernel.efi
The EFI-stub kernel, discovered as a regular boot entry.
.TP
.I \eEFI\eleon\eboot.toml
Boot configuration, read and validated at every boot.
.TP
.I \eEFI\eleon\eentries.jsonc
Discovered boot entries, rewritten every boot.
.TP
.I \eEFI\eleon\ebootinfo.json
Geometry + resolved config record written each boot for
.BR lbt (1).
.TP
.I \evar\elogs\eleon\elog.md
Unified boot log (Markdown, capped at 64 KiB).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lbt (1),
.BR leon-common (7)
